# tomlord.io Project Structure Guide

This is a full-stack project with two main components:

## Backend (tomlord.io-backend/)
- **Language**: Go 1.24.4 with Gin framework
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with pgx driver and SQLC for type-safe queries
- **Main entry**: [cmd/api/main.go](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/cmd/api/main.go)
- **Server logic**: [internal/server/server.go](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/internal/server/server.go) and [internal/server/routes.go](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/internal/server/routes.go)
- **Database layer**: [internal/database/](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/internal/database/) for connection management, [internal/db/](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/internal/db/) for SQLC generated code
- **Authentication**: OAuth with Google using [internal/auth/oauth.go](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/internal/auth/oauth.go) and JWT middleware
- **Services**: Business logic in [internal/services/](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/internal/services/)
- **Docker**: Containerized with [docker-compose.yml](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/docker-compose.yml) and [Dockerfile](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/Dockerfile)

## Frontend (tomlord.io/)
- **Framework**: SvelteKit with Svelte 5 syntax
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4.0
- **Package Manager**: pnpm (NOT npm/yarn)
- **Main config**: [svelte.config.js](mdc:tomlord.io/svelte.config.js) with MDSvex support
- **Content**: Markdown blog posts in [src/markdown/posts/](mdc:tomlord.io/src/markdown/posts/)
- **Routes**: SvelteKit file-based routing in [src/routes/](mdc:tomlord.io/src/routes/)
- **Components**: Reusable components in [src/lib/components/](mdc:tomlord.io/src/lib/components/)
- **API endpoints**: Server-side API routes in [src/routes/api/](mdc:tomlord.io/src/routes/api/)

## Build System
- **Backend**: Uses [Makefile](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/Makefile) for build automation
- **Frontend**: Standard pnpm scripts in [package.json](mdc:tomlord.io/package.json)
- **Database**: Migrations in [migrations/](mdc:tomlord.io-backend/migrations/) directory

